    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1190a-a3">

                <pb facs="1266" n="1170" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1170"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic">April 25,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I confirm my telegram of the 22d instant,
                    reading as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>In the event of hostilities between the United States and Spain the
                            policy of this Government will be not to resort to privateering, but to
                            adhere to the following recognized rules of international law: <list>
                                <item>First. The neutral flag covers enemy’s goods, with the
                                    exception of contraband of war;</item>
                                <pb facs="1267" n="1171" xml:id="pg1171"/>
                                <item>Second. Neutral goods, with the exception of contraband of
                                    war, are not liable to capture under an enemy’s flag, and</item>
                                <item>Third. Blockades in order to be binding must be
                                    effective.</item>
                            </list></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>(To all United States legations abroad.)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
